      "problem": "Given the function \n\n$$\nf(x,w)=4{(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3}+{x}^{T}w\n$$\n\nthat maps a vector to a scalar, find ${∇}_{w}f.$ You may assume that $w$ has no zero components.",
      "worked_solution": "Using the results\n\n$$\n{∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}_{1})=\\text{sign}(w),\\,{∇}_{w}({x}^{T}w)=x,\n$$\n\n we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}f & ={∇}_{w}(4{(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3}+{x}^{T}w) \\\\  & ={∇}_{w}(4{(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3})+{∇}_{w}({x}^{T}w) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {∇}_{w}({(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3})+{∇}_{w}({x}^{T}w) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot {∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}_{1})+x \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)+x \\\\  & =12(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)+x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
